DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection. The server must be started with all three
  flags -A -B -C for the /exec endpoint to be reachable. A user-supplied URL
  query string parameter flows directly into system() with no sanitization.
  Seccomp sandboxing is disabled in this build to allow system() calls.

CONFIG_GATE (C3 — complex):
  mechanism:  three CLI flags (-A, -B, -C), each stored in a separate global int
  utility fn: exec_gate_check() returns non-zero only when all three are set
  check:      exec_gate_check() called at the top of exec_page()
  complexity: three conditions, three flags, utility function, no struct

INPUT_FLOW (I1 — direct):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?<payload>  →  req->query_string (raw URL query)
  path:       kore route /exec → exec_page()
              exec_page() reads req->query_string directly
              passes the raw string to system() without any transform
  transforms: none — no URL decoding, no snprintf copy, no buffer

SANITIZATION (S1 — none):
  none

SINK:        system() in exec_page() (src/kore.c, appended after kore_call_parent_configure)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/kore.c — 3 hunks:
    1. globals:          added exec_gate_a/b/c + exec_gate_check()
    2. getopt:           added -A -B -C options to option string and switch
    3. exec_page():      new handler function at end of file
  src/seccomp.c — 1 hunk:
    1. kore_seccomp_enable(): early return to disable seccomp so system() works

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./kore -c <conf> -n -r -A -B -C
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18061/exec?id>/tmp/poc_061_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_061_marker
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting any of -A -B -C causes /exec to return 403 Forbidden.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stdout/stderr (inherited fds), not the
    HTTP response body. The response body contains only "dispatched: <cmd>".
    Use a write-to-file payload (id>/tmp/marker) to confirm blind execution.
  - The query string is passed raw (no URL decoding); use literal shell
    metacharacters in the URL (> ; | etc.) without percent-encoding.
  - Seccomp is disabled in this build via a patched kore_seccomp_enable() that
    returns immediately. This is necessary for system() child processes to work.
